# Ben's Burger Bar — design

An original cooking game in a cartoon diner. Talking customers order at the counter, and
the player makes each order on an assembly line: the food comes to the player one step at
a time, and every step is one question with one press to answer it. Watching the food cook
is the fun part, and the customers' reactions are the payoff. The game copies no names,
art, characters or mechanics from any other game.

The hub rulebook, `ACCESSIBILITY.md` (hub root), outranks this file. Where the two
disagree, this file is wrong.

This file folds in the **Nov 7 design call** (Ari, Bryan and Tabby; their notes are in
`BURGER-BAR-REDESIGN` beside this file). The call replaced the M1 free-roam station scan
with a guided, phase-based flow. Where the call and the earlier design disagree, the call
wins; [What the redesign changed](#what-the-redesign-changed) lists every reconciled
point, and [Open questions](#open-questions) lists what is still to decide.

**Ben's Food Court (2026-11-08).** The game is now Ben's Food Court: a mall food court of
seven restaurants, each its own game on this engine as a pack, and **Ben's Burger Bar is the
first restaurant and the template for the others**. The folder was renamed from
`BENSBURGERBAR` to `BENSFOODCOURT` (game id `bensfoodcourt`). The proposal for the court, its
restaurants and its build order is `BENS-FOOD-COURT` beside this file (a starting point for
Ari, Bryan and Tabby, with its own open questions). This file stays the Burger Bar's design:
the pattern every restaurant pack follows.

